WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
Happy Monday, welcome to Tesla's short time, episode 533, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.160
It's July 6th, 2026, a new week and plenty happening with Tesla.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.880
Optimus now targets mass production at Fremont by end of 2026 with a long-term goal of

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.560
1 million units annually.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:26.060
Vice President Grace Tao confirmed at the Beijing Global Digital Economy Conference that large-scale

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.840
production will begin by December.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.820
Fremont is the planned initial site, the long-term target is 1 million units per year.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.240
Early output will remain gradual while sublines finish construction.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.120
This moves the program from prototype testing into the first volume phase.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:49.300
Remember that Giga Texas dedicated factory work was already underway as of our last update

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.280
in early July.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.980
The Fremont start date now gives a clearer near-term production window.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:01.740
On the regulatory front, the EUFSD supervised approval process has entered its political

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.160
phase.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:08.200
Germany's Federal Ministry of Transport replied to an inquiry and outlined the remaining steps

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.860
after the June 30 dossier submission.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:16.480
A qualified majority vote at the TCMV Technical Committee comes next.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.940
Once that passes, the Commission can issue an Implementing Act that lets RDW grant approval

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.680
valid across member states.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:31.800
A new EU Advanced Safety Mandate effective July 7 adds fresh documentation requirements right

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.660
before the vote.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:39.840
KBA continues its data review with Tesla and RDW before Germany finalizes its position.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:46.800
While regulators weigh the supervised stack, version 14.3.4 already demonstrates strong

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.460
performance in tough conditions.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:54.220
Tesla shared video of the release navigating heavy rain without any driver intervention.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.840
The clip shows consistent lane keeping and obstacle avoidance through downpours that usually

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.820
challenge camera-based systems.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.980
This continues the V14 series emphasis on edge case weather handling.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:13.280
Listeners tracking FSD progress will watch for the next supervised update that adds documented

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.540
rain handling metrics.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.940
Tesla also posted an owner account of a model Y that carried a phone on its tailgate for

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.820
4.3 miles including highway speeds.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.820
FSD supervised maintained smooth acceleration and braking that kept the device in place.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:36.240
The company used the anecdote to illustrate real-world consistency of the current supervised stack.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.860
The post-drew replies from other owners sharing similar low-speed stability examples.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.920
Real-world examples like this are exactly what owners want reflected in insurance pricing.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:55.540
A change.org petition now asks California regulators to let insurers use Tesla telematics data

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.200
and grant discounts for FSD equipped vehicles.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:05.420
The request argues that current rating models ignore real-world safety data from supervised

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.100
autonomy.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.200
Supporters cite lower claim rates reported by Tesla owners.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.880
The petition remains open for signatures ahead of any insurance department review.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.320
Meanwhile, Tesla is expanding physical infrastructure in another key growth market.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.240
The company installed its first destination charger in Delhi.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:30.360
A new supercharger-style station also opened inside a Delhi shopping mall.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.000
The units support model Y and upcoming right-hand drive vehicles planned for the market.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.220
Local partners handle installation and maintenance.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:45.940
This step follows earlier service center openings and proceeds expected volume deliveries later this year.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.640
Product updates are also helping Tesla refresh its core lineup in established markets.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.840
A longer six-seat model Y variant has reached showrooms.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.820
The stretched model adds a third row bench on the existing model Y platform.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:08.260
Tesla positions it as a lower-cost alternative to the discontinued Model X for families needing six seats.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.640
Production begins on existing lines without major retooling.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:19.080
Early orders in Europe and Japan show interest from buyers who previously considered the larger Model X.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:26.040
Tesla also began deliveries of the longer Model Y L in Japan during the first half of the year.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.300
Registrations through June exceeded the same period last year despite a smaller overall market.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.640
The L model offers extra cargo space behind the third row.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.960
Local inventory levels have dropped faster than expected after the variant launch.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:51.520
An owner reported towing a 4,500-pound air-stream sport trailer with a cyber truck from San Diego to Julian without stopping to charge.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.940
The trip exceeded the range the driver had calculated from earlier non-towing drives.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.760
The cyber trucks on-board energy display showed remaining buffer at arrival.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:07.820
The result adds to owner-collected data on real-world towing efficiency under varying grades.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.580
Even with these updates, recent delivery numbers produced an unexpected market reaction.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.420
Tesla reported 480,126 deliveries for the second quarter.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.840
The figure beat consensus expectations shares fell immediately after the report.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.800
Investors focused on future margins and the pace of energy storage growth.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.680
The reaction followed a pre-report run-up that had priced in much of the beat.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:40.820
Tesla has not yet detailed how production mix or pricing will affect third quarter gross margins.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:48.380
The same regulatory questions affecting FSD also shape how quickly autonomy revenue can scale in Europe.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:57.280
Regulatory approval for supervised autonomy now hinges less on technical validation and more on political consensus among member states.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:09.260
The German Ministry's confirmation that the TCMV vote requires a qualified majority shows the process has moved past RDW technical review into a vote-counting exercise.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:20.120
Tesla's data package is already with regulators. Yet the outcome still depends on how many governments weigh consumer safety arguments against domestic industry concerns.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:30.480
This structure differs from the US approach where individual state DMVs or NHTSA can grant narrower permissions without needing cross-border alignment.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:39.140
In Europe, the Single Implementing Act once passed applies uniformly which lowers the per-country compliance cost if the vote succeeds.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:45.880
The risk is that one or two larger states can block progress even when technical objections have been addressed.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:59.820
For Tesla, the timeline implication is straightforward. Any delay in the TCMV vote directly postpones the revenue ramp from FSD subscriptions and future unsupervised features across the entire EU fleet.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:13.300
The company's European sales already rely on the supervised product. Extending that capability to more markets without repeated national approvals is the clearest near-term margin lever still under regulatory control.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:18.040
In competitive news, a new rival is entering the North American market.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:24.460
Leap motor announced its first North American expansion through Mexico with Stellantis distribution backing.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:34.680
The move positions the Chinese EV maker against Tesla's Model Y and Cybertruck in the region, pricing and model details for Mexico remain under wraps.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.800
The expansion follows Stellantis's earlier investment in the Leap motor brand.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:46.500
Rivian CEO R.J. Scarinj stated publicly that a Tesla takeover is not under discussion.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.640
He emphasized Rivian's independent product roadmap and manufacturing plans.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:57.620
The comment follows weeks of market speculation after both companies beat delivery expectations.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.320
No formal talks have been confirmed by either firm.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:09.040
On the sales side, Model Y topped the second quarter EV registration list at UK Fleet Provider Octopus.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:18.640
The ranking reflects both private and business-least demand. Octopus noted the car's combination of range and charging speed as the main driver.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:28.060
Model Y also leads the Australian EV sales chart through mid-year. Several Chinese brands occupy the next four places on that list.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:34.620
Tesla moved ahead of Hyundai in Korean EV registrations for the first time in the current sales year.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:40.080
The shift comes as Model Y inventory cleared faster than local competitors stock.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.420
Hyundai dealers reported increased discounting pressure in response.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:50.300
Market share data for June showed Tesla at roughly one fifth of total EV sales.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:56.140
Keep an eye on the next TCMV vote outcome and any fresh optimist production updates.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.260
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:09.100
TSLA closed at $393.45 down $31.85, 7.5%.

